293
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:28,233
a drug maker's profit,

294
00:10:28,233 --> 00:10:30,157
an insurer's revenue.

295
00:10:30,237 --> 00:10:32,521
Lowering the price means someone gets paid

296
00:10:32,521 --> 00:10:32,955
less,

297
00:10:32,955 --> 00:10:35,239
and each of them has every reason

298
00:10:35,239 --> 00:10:36,525
to fight it.

299
00:10:36,784 --> 00:10:39,522
So why do Americans pay so much

300
00:10:39,522 --> 00:10:40,944
for health care?

301
00:10:41,234 --> 00:10:43,025
Not because they go to the doctor

302
00:10:43,025 --> 00:10:43,744
more.

303
00:10:43,744 --> 00:10:45,094
They go less.

304
00:10:45,194 --> 00:10:47,559
They pay more for each visit,

305
00:10:47,559 --> 00:10:48,428
each scan,

306
00:10:48,428 --> 00:10:49,296
each pill,

307
00:10:49,296 --> 00:10:50,794
and each claim.

308
00:10:50,884 --> 00:10:53,221
Health care in America is not expensive

309
00:10:53,221 --> 00:10:55,574
because of how much care people get.

310
00:10:55,684 --> 00:10:58,602
It is expensive because of what each

311
00:10:58,602 --> 00:11:00,369
piece of care costs.

312
00:11:00,617 --> 00:11:03,108
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

313
00:11:03,108 --> 00:11:06,079
we follow the money behind another hidden

314
00:11:06,079 --> 00:11:08,507
link of the world economy.

315
00:11:08,747 --> 00:11:10,647
This is The Hidden Economics.
